# loss — Ring-1 stratum: the declared costs maps-to edges carry (C9)
stratum loss "Loss terms for maps-to edges: what a lossy translation gives up. A loss term names the cost; the matcher accumulates the path (C9)."

term loss "The @loss attribute key on maps-to: which loss this translation incurs."
term visual-only "Semantic content survives only as appearance; machine meaning is dropped."
term ordinal-coarsening "A finer ordinal scale collapses onto a coarser one; distinctions inside a bucket are lost (F28: the hole round 5 found — added)."
term unit-mismatch "Values converted across units with rounding; exact magnitudes are not recoverable."
term precision-loss "Numeric precision reduced (fewer digits, wider buckets)."
